geometry                                         geometry-V11-04-03
--------
- divisions (geomdiv-V11-04-01)
  o In G4PVDivision and G4ReplicatedSlice, adapted to new scheme of providing
    a separate, per-thread instances of a logical volume's solid, material,
    mass and cuts-couple attributes. For the new split-class mechanism
    (trigerred at runtime) these classes signal the need to use separate
    per-thread state by calling G4LogicalVolume::MarkMaterialMutable().
  o In G4ReplicatedSlice, enhanced parameter checks in the constructor;
    CheckAndSetParameters() takes a non-const 'pLogical', so it can mark the
    logical volume mutable.
- magneticfield (field-V11-04-01)
  o Preserve concrete stepper types in G4FieldSetup: construct type-specific
    integration drivers for built-in field steppers instead of instantiating
    their drivers with G4MagIntegratorStepper as the template parameter:
    create G4IntegrationDriver<ConcreteStepper> for regular steppers; retain
    type-specific FSAL driver construction; use polymorphic fallback for
    user-provided steppers; support both magnetic and electromagnetic field
    configurations; correct driver ownership during repeated field updates.
- management (geommng-V11-04-11)
  o In G4LogicalVolume, refined the storage of key attributes which are
    constant during simulation for specific volumes types, i.e. logical
    volumes used only in placement and replicas physical volumes.
    The attributes are the solid, material, and cuts-couple pointers, and the
    value of the mass; for these instances the 'master' value is always used
    and a slot for "per-thread" values is NOT created.
    Logical volumes used by "varying" physical volumes (parameterised,
    divisions, replicated slices) are marked as "mutable" and maintain a
    per-thread (split) instance of the attributes, as they can have
    multiple values.
  o Added a class, G4ParameterisationChecker, which checks for a parameterised
    replica-family logical volume which is inconsistent with orthodox
    expectations (e.g. a parameterisation keeps the same logical volume for
    all daughter volumes). Marks these as "mutable" and provides (temporary)
    work-around.
  o Added a shared recursive polyhedron-cache mutex in G4VSolid to avoid lock
    ordering deadlocks for nested solids. Documented cache lifetime constraints.
  o Fixed GetPolyhedron() cache locking in G4UAdapter and G4ReflectedSolid;
    delete the old reflected polyhedron when rebuilding.
  o Fixed verbosity handling in G4GeometryManager and G4VoxelisationHelper   (o)
    to print voxel statistics and the global timing report once through the
    master after MT voxelisation, preserving explicit verbosity requests
    without additional diagnostic printouts.
  o Avoid duplicate tree search done in G4RunManagerKernel::CheckRegions() by
    adding a Boolean return value to G4Region::SetWorld(). to indicate if the
    volume is placed in the world or not.
- navigation (geomnav-V11-04-09)
  o Added a new class, G4GeometryMemoryAdvisor, to analyses a constructed
    geometry and report how many distinct logical volumes are either
    "mutable" (daughter of a G4PVParameterised, G4PVDivision, or a
    G4ReplicatedSlice), and so carry per-thread attributes, versus "shared"
    (everything else, sharing those fields across all threads with no
    per-thread storage for them). The class also reports the per-thread
    LV-side memory this geometry actually uses, and the amount saved.
  o Extended G4LogicalVolumeUsageVisitor to count physical volume types.
    Extended G4VTouchableVisitor and G4TouchableWalker to 'Regular' Structures.
  o In G4VolumeTreeWalker, fixed undefined behaviour in dispatch with did not
    correctly distinguish between the three independent sibling physical
    volume subclasses.
  o Added new checker class G4ParameterisationCheckVisitor, exercising every
    parameterisation, including ones nested inside one or two replica levels.
  o G4Navigator: fixed a bug in CreateTouchableHistory() when the current    (o)
    location is outside the world volume.
  o Added helper method CheckAndConfirmTouchable() in G4Navigator, which
    undertakes a check of candidate touchable, corrects the location if it is
    in another volumes and reports if position is outside the world volume.
    Added auxiliary methods ReportOutsidePoint().
  o In G4VoxelNavigation, added consistency checks in ComputeStep() and
    ComputeSafety(), that internal data (VoxelStack) is up-to-date with the
    current volume's voxel header (if not correct, fix it before proceeding);
    ensure that daughter indices found in voxel data structures are within
    bounds; a warning is issued when either problem occurs, with frequency
    reducing; navigation proceeds, with a corrective action.
- solids/Boolean (geom-bool-V11-04-07)
  o Copy owned displaced operands independently in Boolean copy construction
    and assignment, preventing clone destruction from invalidating the original.
  o Fixed GetPolyhedron() cache races in G4BooleanSolid, G4MultiUnion,
    G4DisplacedSolid and G4ScaledSolid using the shared recursive mutex,
    allowing nested-solid access without lock ordering deadlocks.
    Delete old displaced and scaled polyhedra when rebuilding their caches.
  o Corrected union normals at hidden operand edges and distant Boolean entry
    queries. Fixed cached interval offsets and progression in intersection
    traversal, avoiding zero entry distances on iteration exhaustion.
  o In G4SubtractionSolid, preserve operand A entries rounded outside its
    surface when operand B is outside, preventing missed subtraction
    intersections.
  o Accelerated G4MultiUnion accurate DistanceToIn(p) safety with a component
    bounding-box hierarchy: measured 47x/192x/54x gains for grid/chain or
    rotated-grid layouts at 16,384 components; worst-case query complexity
    remains O(N). Reused cached voxel candidates and reentrant thread-local
    entry scratch, eliminating measured warmed-query allocations. At 16,384
    components, local navigation gained 6-20x and longitudinal chain exits 12x,
    with approximately linear measured chain-exit scaling (N^1.08 over
    64-16,384 components). Cached bounds during voxelization, making
    BoundingLimits/CalculateExtent O(1) afterwards; invalidate on AddNode and
    rebuild on re-voxelization.
    With updated G4Voxelizer for solids, G4MultiUnion retained memory at 16,384
    components fell from 132.8 to 4.66 MB for overlapping chains and from 4.52
    to 3.93 MB for separated grids; both measured approximately N^1.01 scaling
    over 64-16,384 components. Coarsening can increase candidate counts for
    dense or irregular layouts. Preserved accurate-safety mode during outside
    SurfaceNormal() queries.
- solids/CSG (geom-csg-V11-04-03)
  o G4Tubs, G4Cons, G4CutTubs: account for angular tolerance in phi exits
    and code refactoring. Corrected near-axis and corner ray intersections
    and classification of nearly full phi spans. Corrected the inner-cone exit
    side and normal validity in G4Cons, and oblique phi-face areas in G4CutTubs.
  o G4Tubs: corrected grazing departures from tolerated phi surfaces and
    distant cylinder entries when cancellation erases the discriminant. Accept
    tolerated outward entries at the inner cylinder, avoiding potential missed
    cut boundaries in subtraction exits.
  o G4Cons: clamp tolerated outward departures before checking intersections
    and retain shallow exits. Handle rounded outer-surface tangencies.
    Fixed case of spurious entry on axial ray thorugh cone apex.
    Stabilise distant tube/cone entries before evaluating radial roots.
    Corrected tube exits through the axis and phi normals at the axis.
  o G4Sphere: fixed negative distances in DistanceToOut() for cone-parallel
    rays by rejecting backward and wrong-half-cone theta intersections.
    Based on [GitHub PR #116](https://github.com/Geant4/geant4/pull/116).
    Fixed DistanceToOut for a wide-phi (>pi) sphere starting on a
    phi cut plane, which could report the outer-sphere distance for a ray
    that immediately leaves the valid wedge.
  o G4Torus: condition distant ray entries at the bounding box to avoid missed
    intersections and inaccurate entry distances for thin tori.
  o G4Box: little optimisation in DistanceToIn(p,v) and DistanceToOut(p,v).
  o Reworked G4Para directional distance queries in its oblique box frame,
    replacing repeated side-plane clipping with three slab intersections and
    direct exit-face selection. Shared the exit traversal between normal and
    no-normal queries to avoid duplicated code.
  o Fixed DCLP thread-safety in G4CSGSolid::GetPolyhedron() by holding the
    shared recursive mutex across cache checks, rebuilding and pointer
    retrieval.
  o G4UTrap: fixed the Right Angular Wedge constructor passing an
    already-computed slope where VecGeom's UnplacedTrapezoid expects an
    angle and applies its own tangent, shearing the wedge incorrectly.
- solids/specific (geom-specific-V11-04-10)
  o Improved G4Polycone/G4Polyhedra safety scaling with a compact RZ bounds
    hierarchy, retaining direct scans for short profiles.
    Localised horizontal-edge checks in Inside() to the relevant Z slabs.
    Use linear lookup for short Z-slab tables and extend phi-face rejection
    to short polyhedra normal queries, preserving near-tie comparisons.
    Improved exit safety with local Z-ordered contour searches, retaining
    the RZ bounds tree for long profiles.
    Bypass azimuth selection in one-sided polyhedra Inside() and safety
    queries, with conservative phi-face rejection for short profiles.
    Fixed grazing cone intersections and cap rounding, retaining a common
    solver for sensitive two-plane exits with and without normals.
    Corrected polycone phi-cut exits and rotated full-phi polyhedra bounds.
  o In G4Polyhedra, fixed SurfaceNormal() on slanted lateral facets; the
    cos(halfPhi) foreshortening of the RZ-profile normal was applied to the
    radial instead of the z component, tilting normals by a few degrees.
    Fixed Inside() classification beyond finite RZ profile edges.
  o Fixed G4Polycone entry safety on phi cuts and surface exits in two-plane
    profiles. Corrected normal validity on concave radial boundaries.
    Corrected grazing and distant-ray intersections in G4Polycone and
    G4IntersectingCone. Retain tolerated entries at finite cylinder/cone
    joins in the shared polycone intersection solver, including
    G4GenericPolycone.
  o In G4GenericPolycone, fixed cap-adjacent convex RZ classification and
    consequent safety overestimates; retain indexed classification for long
    profiles.
  o In G4Hype, fixed DistanceToIn(p,v) accepting a root of the hyperbolic
    surface far beyond halfLenZ when an endplate crossing was certified,
    returning a distance shorter than the safety for distant rays.
    Corrected the inner-surface normal test in DistanceToIn(p,v), which used
    the outer stereo angle. Rays entering the material through the inner
    hyperbolic surface could be rejected, returning 'kInfinity' for a crossing
    that exists.
  o Corrected the surface relation used by G4Paraboloid::DistanceToIn(p)
    safety. The safety could exceed the true distance to the solid, so a step
    of one safety could reach material.
  o Corrected G4EllipticalTube zero-distance exit normals to use the original
    ellipse coordinates in both outgoing and grazing lateral-surface branches.
    Preserve small transverse components in near-axis rays.
  o In G4ExtrudedSolid, accelerated polygon queries and exact entry with edge
    rejection, cap shortcuts and convex Z-slab clipping, prioritising small
    prisms. Measured gains: Inside 1.5-1.8x and exact entry/exit 2.2x/2.1x.
    Improved scaling over the number of facets; large-mesh construction gained
    9-15x over earlier native versions, with up to 55x less heap in the tested
    toroidal mesh. Retain unambiguous vertex exits from non-convex right
    prisms, avoiding missed tessellated intersections that returned a zero exit
    distance. Corrected grazing exits starting just outside a non-convex prism.
  o Fixed DCLP thread-safety in all GetPolyhedron() implementations by holding
    the shared recursive mutex across cache checks, rebuilding and pointer
    retrieval, replacing local polyhedron mutexes.
  o Accelerated navigation in G4TessellatedSolid and G4QuadrangularFacet
    queries using geometry caches and hierarchies, preserving finite-surface
    safety and tolerance handling. Code cleanup.
    Fixed missed voxel entries, copying/reopening and shared scratch handling.
    Recorded speedups over original native navigation (geometric means):
    tessellated Inside 2-74x, normals 3.9x, exit safety 9.4x and exact
    entry/exit 1.2x/8.2x.
  o Replaced dense G4Voxelizer masks for solids with bounded cell candidate
    lists, coarsening the grid as needed for O(N) retained and temporary
    storage. Added direct point lookup and preserved candidate exclusions
    and diagnostics. Helps in improving memory scaling in G4MultiUnion
    structures. Fixed false-positive compilation warnings for uninitialised
    data on Linux.
  o Removed a redundant vertex copy in G4GenericTrap assignment operator.
  o Corrected twisted-faceted exit normals and directional intersections,
    including certified high-twist vertical crossings and fixed
    assignments to release old constituent surfaces before rebuilding.
  o Accelerated G4TwistedTubs::Inside() with immutable cached bounds and
    direct radial, phi and endcap classification, retaining the legacy path
    for directly persisted objects; measured about 5.0x for Inside() and a
    further 1.2x for directional exact distances and SurfaceNormal across
    the benchmarked topologies. Code cleanup.
  o Accelerated faceted solids (G4TwistedBox, Trap and Trd) Inside, safety,
    SurfaceNormal and exact-distance queries with immutable untwisted-face
    data, early candidate rejection, allocation-free storage and a certified
    first-root solver with exact fallbacks. Measured about 7.0x for
    DistanceToIn(p,v) and 12.0x for both DistanceToOut(p,v) variants.
    Code cleanup.
